Carry a response requirement through realization and inspection (@engineering-realization-evidence: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Investigate-compatible-members-stored-energy-and-ambiguous-movement.lingua#r_00B6630CABB33AE7E80B90B9EE") { r_00B6F25CACF583F02249520A8B
A response calculation becomes useful engineering knowledge when its parameters and assumptions can be connected to an actual object. Return to [Connect realization to verification and intended use](Connect-realization-to-verification-and-intended-use.lingua#r_0C593F4A7A204FABB3B5876653) and [Propagate dimensional limits through a signed assembly model](Propagate-dimensional-limits-through-a-signed-assembly-model.lingua#r_0E388D8E2EC1D967485C09A648). Preserve the requirement's reference locations, load and environment, the selected geometry, the material state and the interface constraints. A drawing revision, replacement material or changed attachment may invalidate an earlier response calculation even when a part still fits.

Read [Systems Engineering Handbook — NASA](../mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/sources/Systems-Engineering-Handbook-NASA.lingua#r_7ZQFZ9E1NAVG27SE2R5S24PDBQ) progressively in sections 5.1–5.2 for implementation choices and interface integration. Use the reasoning about connecting a realized configuration to its requirements and evidence; institutional flight-project procedures retain their own context. For our original axial example, the questions are whether the intended sections and reference lengths were realized, whether the properties and free-strain account describe the supplied material, and whether the attachments impose the assumed relative motion. Keep predicted results distinct from performed observations.

Consider the model δ=(P+k₂g)/(k₁+k₂) with g₁=0. Stipulate a bounded input box: P∈[380,420] N, k₁∈[0.9,1.1]×10⁶ N/m, k₂∈[2.7,3.3]×10⁶ N/m and g∈[30,50] μm. These are hypothetical hard bounds, not measured distributions. δ increases with P and g. It decreases with k₁ because P+k₂g>0; its derivative with respect to k₂ is (gk₁−P)/(k₁+k₂)²<0 throughout the box, since gk₁≤55 N<380 N. These signs justify the endpoint extrema rather than assuming every nonlinear model reaches its extrema at box corners.

The lower extension is 479/(4,400,000) m, about 108.86 μm; the upper is 37/240000 m, about 154.17 μm. A nominal prediction of 130 μm meets the illustrative δ≤150 μm criterion, but the full box does not establish it for every allowed input. The box may also include physically impossible combinations if parameters share causes; adding that information requires evidence. Do not turn the box into a confidence interval.

An explicitly hypothetical alternative increases both stiffnesses and their bounds by 20%, leaving load, lengths and free extensions unchanged. The same monotonic argument gives maximum 97/720000 m, about 134.72 μm. One modeled way is to increase both cross-sectional areas by 20% at the same E and L, increasing their material volume by 20%; the geometry, interfaces and realizability must then be reassessed. This passes only the stated displacement screen. It does not establish strength, stability, manufacturing capability, cost, endurance or real material properties.

**Work:** prepare a compact evidence record mapping each influential parameter and connection assumption to its provenance, proposed observation and revision trigger. Include an unverified property, a changed section and a conflicting measurement. Explain what evidence the numerical alternative adds and what remains missing. Broader production engineering, process capability, maintenance and recovery remain necessary next layers; clean manufacturing remains one later production specialization.

